  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Change of MS Junior Project Leader (France, INSEE)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;The National Institute of Statistics (NIS) of Cambodia, which is part of the Ministry of Planning, is responsible for the coordination of the National Statistical System, which is key to inform and improve government work, public policy, financial management, particularly the budgeting process, and monitoring and evaluation of public policies. As Cambodia moves towards a performance informed budgeting, it will be increasingly important for the government to be able to demonstrate actual impact of policies by using statistics. The overall objectives to support to the National Institute of Statistics are:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;- &amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Improve the quality and timeliness of economic and financial statistical data including the collection and analysis with gender responsive approach&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Support the implementation of the National Strategy for the Development of Statistics, including the improvement of socioeconomic statistics highlighting gender issues;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;ql-align-justify&quot;&gt;-&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;Strengthen the capacity of the Government of Cambodia conducive to the implementation of PFM policies;&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
